:\n\\[ x^2 - 4x - 21 \\leq 0. \\]\nFactoring the quadratic expression, we get:\n\\[ (x-7)(x+3) \\leq 0. \\]\nThe roots are \\( x = 7 \\) and \\( x = -3 \\), so the solution to the inequality is:\n\\[ -3 \\leq x \\leq 7. \\]\n\n2. For the second term, \\(\\sqrt{-x^2 + 3x + 10}\\), we solve the inequality:\n\\[ -x^2 + 3x + 10 \\geq 0. \\]\nRewriting, we get:\n\\[ x^2 - 3x - 10 \\leq 0. \\]\nFactoring the quadratic expression, we get:\n\\[ (x-5)(x+2) \\leq 0. \\]\nThe roots are \\( x = 5 \\) and \\( x = -2 \\), so the solution to the inequality is:\n\\[ -2 \\leq x \\leq 5. \\]\n\nThe domain of \\( f(x) \\) is the intersection of the two intervals:\n\\[ -2 \\leq x \\leq 5. \\]\n\nNext, we analyze the function \\( f(x) \\) within this domain. We will check the values of \\( f(x) \\) at the endpoints and potentially at critical points within the domain.\n\n- At \\( x = -2 \\):\n\\[ f(-2) = \\sqrt{-(-2)^2 + 4(-2) + 21} - \\sqrt{-(-2)^2 + 3(-2) + 10} = \\sqrt{-4 - 8 + 21} - \\sqrt{-4 - 6 + 10} = \\sqrt{9} - \\sqrt{0} = 3 - 0 = 3. \\]\n\n- At \\( x = 5 \\):\n\\[ f(5) = \\sqrt{-(5)^2 + 4(5) + 21} - \\sqrt{-(5)^2 + 3(5) + 10} = \\sqrt{-25 + 20 + 21} - \\sqrt{-25 + 15 + 10} = \\sqrt{16} - \\sqrt{0} = 4 - 0 = 4. \\]\n\n- At \\( x = 0 \\):\n\\[ f(0) = \\sqrt{-(0)^2 + 4(0) + 21} - \\sqrt{-(0)^2 + 3(0) + 10} = \\sqrt{21} - \\sqrt{10}. \\]\nSince \\( \\sqrt{21} \\approx 4.58 \\) and \\( \\sqrt{10} \\approx 3.16 \\), we have:\n\\[ f(0) \\approx 4.58 - 3.16 = 1.42. \\]\n\n- At \\( x = 3 \\):\n\\[ f(3) = \\sqrt{-(3)^2 + 4(3) + 21} - \\sqrt{-(3)^2 + 3(3) + 10} = \\sqrt{-9 + 12 + 21} - \\sqrt{-9 + 9 + 10} = \\sqrt{24} - \\sqrt{10} = 2\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{10}. \\]\nSince \\( 2\\sqrt{6} \\approx 4.899 \\) and \\( \\sqrt{10} \\approx 3.162 \\), we have:\n\\[ f(3) \\approx 4.899 - 3.162 = 1.737. \\]\n\nFrom the above calculations, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) is at \\( x = -2 \\) and is \\( 3 \\).\n\nThus, the minimum value of the function is \\(\\boxed{3}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{3}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
